        "original_id": "4332a15f-09bb-5078-a4b8-cea2717e23f5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Charles Spitzka, Charles Guiteau, James A. Garfield\n- Roles: neurologist, medical specialist in mental diseases, assassin, President of the United States\n- Events: Guiteau's murder trial, assassination of James A. Garfield\n\nFacts:\n- James A. Garfield was the 20th President of the United States and served from March 4, 1881, until his assassination later in 1881.\n- In 1881, Edward Charles Spitzka was a famous neurologist and medical specialist in mental diseases.\n- In 1881, Edward Charles Spitzka testified that Charles Guiteau was insane at Guiteau's murder trial.\n- Charles Guiteau was the assassin of President James A. Garfield.",
